WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.480
The seasonal uniform change!

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.560
It's been so muggy lately, you know?

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.570
Even just changing into short sleeves
feels much more comfortable.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.110
Right.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
RESPONSIBILITY AND DUTY

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.540
Relationship advice?

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.250
Yes! I don't know what to do.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.340
But I heard that the student council
gives advice for that kind of thing, too.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:58.970
KAGUYA WANTS TO HANDLE IT

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.390
You're the only one I can count on,
Miss Kaguya!

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.720
Understood.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:06.060
The president here often says
that lending an ear to the students' troubles

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.350
is also a duty of the student council.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:09.850
So,

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.360
what's the trouble?

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.110
I want to know how to break up
smoothly with my boyfriend.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.870
<i>I thought it would be
two or three steps before that point!</i>

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.450
<i>Advice about having a boyfriend.</i>

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.460
You're really popular, and I'm sure
you know a lot about love!

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:36.960
<i>But I've never even gone out with anyone,
so how could I possibly answer that?</i>

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.960
I knew I could come to you
for a great idea!

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.970
<i>Her expectations are too high!</i>

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.300
<i>But Shinomiya gave romantic advice once,</i>

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.640
<i>so there's no way
I can tell her it's beyond me!</i>

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.600
<i>I'll just have to get through it somehow!</i>

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.350
Why do you want to break up?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.610
Actually, he suddenly asked me out.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.440
<i>Bam!</i>

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.150
I said, "Okay" on the spur of the moment,

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.530
but I didn't really know him.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.120
And I don't really know
how to communicate with him either.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.200
In fact, there's more distance
between us now than before.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.580
I feel guilty about it,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.630
so if it's going to be like this, I figured
maybe we're better off just breaking up.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.250
I see.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.970
Until just before,
you were strangers to each other.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.840
So I can see where you're coming from.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.720
You don't hate him, though, do you?

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:31.480
Of course not. But I don't know
if what I feel for him is love.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.230
Why don't you start
by telling me his good points?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.780
What I like about him?

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:41.860
Yes. Everyone has strong points
or something that's cute about them.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.120
For example, he's honest
or he does well academically.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.120
Maybe he studies hard
or he's actually really kind

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.580
and can't turn his back
on someone who's in trouble.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.340
Maybe he has a menacing look.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.300
A menacing look is a drawback.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.510
No! Being bothered
by your own menacing look is cute!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.100
You like boys who have menacing looks?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.600
Forget I said that.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.890
The only person around you
with a menacing look that I can think of...

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.400
That's the wrong idea.
Now let's continue.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:21.110
If you find one good thing about him
and start to appreciate that,

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.530
you'll soon be able to see
many of his good points,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.990
and the next thing you know,
you're unable to take your eyes off of him.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.660
And if you see him every day...

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.870
little by little, you'll fall in love.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.670
That's what an acquaintance told me!

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.500
I'm not talking about me!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.670
Really?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.300
It's really not about me!

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.720
Because there isn't anyone
I'm in love with!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.380
But the way you said it...

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.720
I overheard!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.890
Miss Fujiwara?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.760
It's no fair to have girls' talk without me!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.350
Please leave an issue like that
to Love Detective Chika!

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.350
LOVE DETECTIVE CHIKA

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.520
Why are you breathing hard?

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.190
Actually, I was here from the beginning,

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.030
but made a mad dash to the drama club
to borrow this costume.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.870
You're in a quandary, because you can't
find your feelings for him.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:09.950
Right?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.080
Yes.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.330
Then this great detective will find
that lost property called "love"

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.920
and return it to you.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.380
So, imagine him flirting with another girl.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.010
What is this?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.260
Just try to imagine it.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.430
Gloomy.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.430
GLOOMY...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.440
Grrr.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.310
GRRR GRRR

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.190
I didn't like that feeling.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.440
Right?

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.650
In other words, that's jealousy.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.610
You don't like that image
because you like him.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.200
The more unpleasant the feeling,
the deeper the love!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.080
Love?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:06:00.250
So, you also like him, Miss Kashiwagi.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.330
No, there's no way.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.590
I don't feel that way about the president,
right? I mean, come on.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.590
You should take that feeling
and nurture it.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.130
I see.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.180
I suspected myself of being a cold person
for not being able to fall in love with someone

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.050
who went as far as professing
his love for me.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:11.890
But...

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.640
you're right! I actually do love him!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.600
<i>It's like she was talked into it!</i>

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:24.730
What should I do
to talk to him more naturally?

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.730
<i>I have to give
more appropriate advice, too!</i>

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.360
Good question.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.650
Cognitive balance.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.240
You can probably use
the Romeo and Juliet effect.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.370
- Romeo and Juliet?
- Romeo and Juliet?

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.120
Romeo and Juliet's love faced obstacles.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.620
The idea is that love deepens

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.630
when a couple shares
a powerful enemy they face.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.760
A powerful enemy?

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.130
It doesn't have to be a person.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.760
A shared imaginary enemy is fine.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.760
We don't have an enemy like that.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:58.180
Oh no! Everyone has
a powerful enemy they have to face!

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.520
Wh-Who?

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.520
It's...

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.400
this society!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.270
Society?

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.360
Unending war! The ever-expanding gap
between rich and poor!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.860
There are no enemies
more powerful than that!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.950
<i>Wait. It should be something minor
like entrance exams or everyday troubles.</i>

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:17.370
I-I see! So the two of us
should rebel against this corrupt society!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.910
<i>That's a large-scale challenge!</i>

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.120
Understood!
The two of us will prepare!

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.040
Good luck!

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.920
Wait! Hold on!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.800
Will it be okay? Did we just create
two antisocial deviants?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.800
It'll be fine!

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.810
Please donate to the fund!

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.940
Please!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:45.230
Please donate to the fund!

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.070
It seems they were both
already interested in charity work.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.400
Please!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.820
This has become a good opportunity.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.110
The feeling of wishing for peace...

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:57.540
That may be the true meaning
of rebelling against society.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.790
What are you talking about?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.040
<i>So, her boyfriend is the one
who went to the president for advice.</i>

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.380
President?

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.300
Shinomiya!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.430
Why are you here with them?

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.890
Oh, I applied to do
off-campus fundraising activities.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:25.440
Please donate to the fund!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.310
Well, when I saw those two who don't seem
to be doing it on a whim or as a pastime,

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.570
Please!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.020
who are inexperienced but eager...

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.440
Please donate to the fund!

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.950
it made me feel like supporting them
even if it's not much.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.950
Please!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.700
Jeez.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:37.450
Please donate to the fund!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.370
This kind of activity
really isn't up my alley, though.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.450
Please!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.210
This is one of the things.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.960
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.500
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.960
KAGUYA LOSES

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.960
Kaguya loses.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.960
PLEASE DONATE TO THE FUND

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.960
PLEASE

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.800
MIYUKI SHIROGANE
WANTS TO SHOW OFF

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:04.730
WHACK

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.150
<i>I was so close!</i>

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.690
<i>Not athletic!</i>

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.690
NOTE: NOT ATHLETIC

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.160
<i>When it comes to studying,
Shirogane excels,</i>

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.950
<i>but as for athletics, he's a catastrophe,
unfit for any human to see.</i>

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:25.870
<i>He delivered newspapers for many years,
and in the summertime, worked as a mover.</i>

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:29.460
<i>He's easily able to ride his bike
the 15 kilometers to school every day.</i>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:33.130
<i>Miyuki Shirogane definitely doesn't suffer
from a lack of physical ability.</i>

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:38.090
<i>He just has an alarming lack
of coordination! That's the cause!</i>

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.260
<i>So, in order to protect
his social status at Shuchiin Academy,</i>

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.100
<i>daily extraordinary training is essential!</i>

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.690
<i>We've got volleyball next week.</i>

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.320
<i>I have to get to the point
of average ability by then.</i>

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.320
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.240
<i>Please take this seriously.</i>

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.820
<i>It looks like a dying alpaca,
but is that the president?</i>

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:58.820
<i>Really?</i>

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.160
<i>That dying alpaca?</i>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.870
<i>How cute.</i>

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.040
No!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.670
Why isn't this working?

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.420
President, are you okay?

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.920
Yeah, no prob...

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.550
Fujiwara!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.630
What are you doing?

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:21.510
I forgot this here. Um...

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.890
<i>Did she see me?</i>

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.230
<i>It's over.
Good at both sports and studies...</i>

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:31.150
<i>The well-rounded
President Shirogane brand...</i>

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:36.320
<i>Even though I didn't do anything wrong,
my flawless image will...</i>

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:39.280
<i>Did I study for the test? Not really.</i>

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.910
This is really bad.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.620
Playing with a ball is so much fun!

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:46.870
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.370
<i>Whatever she thinks about me,
it won't do much damage.</i>

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.880
Volleyball is the next sport for P.E., right?

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.960
I was able to reserve the gym,
so I've been practicing.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.220
My serve is kind of weak, you know?

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.880
Oh, I see.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.680
Want me to teach you?

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:07.640
Look, you can't teach someone
unless you can do it yourself.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.390
I'm okay at volleyball!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:11.520
See?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:14.770
Right?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:16.190
Incredible!

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.530
PRESIDENT'S CRITERIA

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.530
How could her serve be so polished?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.030
How'd you like that?

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:23.320
I-I had no idea you possessed
such a special skill!

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.580
I bet if I taught you,
you'd improve in no time.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:35.880
GRIN GRIN

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.460
President! When you're
asking someone for help,

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.130
what kind of attitude is appropriate?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:40.220
P-Please teach me.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.470
Sure! No problem!

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.010
Okay, first let me see
exactly what the problem is.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:48.770
Please show me your serve several times.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.180
Okay.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.490
Why does that happen?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.700
I don't know myself.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.490
No matter how many times I try,
I keep hitting myself in the head.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.460
And if I'm careful about my head,
my timing is totally off.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.500
I'm perfectly deadlocked!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.170
Right.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.800
First of all, when you hit the ball,
keep your eyes open!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.880
You don't have to state the obvious.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.680
Right, right!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.680
Then open your eyes wide
and try to hit the ball.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.310
As if that would make a difference.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.400
See? That didn't work.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:38.650
Your eyes aren't open!

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.400
They're not open!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.280
How can you project the feeling,
"I did what you said, but it didn't work"?

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:46.620
Look! They weren't even open
one millimeter!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.280
I don't believe it!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.410
Maybe I have what they call "the yips"?

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:52.540
What arrogance!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:57.290
President, maybe your image of yourself
isn't in sync with your actual movements!

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.550
Let's start with jumping
with your eyes open!

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.590
I'm going to be merciless with you,
so be prepared!

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:04.430
Please!

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.890
OGRE

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.470
<i>And so...</i>

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:09.140
1, 2,

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.930
3, 4 ,5...

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.060
556, 557, 558, 559...

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.150
<i>984, 985, 986 ,987...</i>

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.150
No closed eyes when you jump.
The ball is your friend.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:22.400
<i>And so, with morning and evening
training sessions, three days passed.</i>

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:26.860
President...

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.120
Maybe this is enough.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.870
I think you're good enough to be
at the level of a person who just sucks at it.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:36.750
Compared to when you were a creature,
you've made a lot of progress.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:37.710
Not yet!

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.750
I can still...

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.340
do more!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.630
Why are you working so hard for this?

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:47.130
Because I don't want them
to see me look like a dork.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.890
If they're going to see me,
I want them to see me look cool!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.980
Are you talking
about the person you like, President?

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.570
Not at all!
You've got romance on the brain!

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:05.030
You don't have to hide it from me!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:05.990
Who's she? Who's she?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:06.740
Shut up!

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.240
Please tell me!

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.570
Don't pester me about that!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.460
Y-You did it!

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:22.340
You did it! You did it!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.960
Yeah, Fujiwara. Thanks to you.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:29.890
It was so tough!
But you persevered until you achieved it!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.300
All right, Fujiwara.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.470
Next teach me how to toss and receive!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.900
ONE WEEK LATER

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.030
Wow!

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.110
Shirogane!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:14:59.920
Miss Fujiwara?

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.710
I raised that boy.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.710
You're his mother?

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:09.970
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.710
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.340
<i>Shirogane and Fujiwara's victory!</i>

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.970
SHIROGANE AND
FUJIWARA'S VICTORY

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:12.720
YES, WELL...

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:13.970
I'LL NEVER DO IT AGAIN.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:21.350
KAGUYA WANTS TO BE COVERED

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:21.350
All right. Ishigami finished dealing
with the aftermath of that last mixer...

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.360
so there really isn't anything
for us to do today.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:25.900
Shall we take the day off?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:29.360
Sure! Then you'd better call
for an early pickup, Miss Kaguya.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.860
Actually...

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:35.370
the car has a flat or something,
so I thought I'd walk home.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.040
You won't be kidnapped?

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.960
Not much evidence is left on a rainy day,
so that's when they target you!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:45.170
Please don't say things
that'll make me nervous.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.960
I'd like to give you a lift,
but I have somewhere to go.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.180
<i>Shinomiya is going to walk home?</i>

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.180
That's okay.
I appreciate the sentiment.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.430
<i>Then maybe that'll work?</i>

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.100
<i>The turning point of the season.
The rainy season.</i>

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.810
<i>Sharing an umbrella!</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.940
<i>Two shoulders close together
under one umbrella,</i>

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:03.940
<i>an event that immediately closes
the distance between man and woman.</i>

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.690
<i>The rainy season is the ideal season
to share an umbrella.</i>

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.440
<i>What nonsense.</i>

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:12.700
<i>Shamefully jostling each other
under one umbrella...</i>

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:17.990
<i>But I do recognize the meaning
behind sharing an umbrella.</i>

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:20.330
<i>In the realm of romance,
what should be feared the most</i>

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.210
<i>is summer vacation magic.</i>

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.580
<i>"Spending summer vacation
with your sweetheart."</i>

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.710
<i>That brand is so sought after</i>

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.170
<i>that before summer vacation starts,
evaluation of the opposite sex</i>

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.720
<i>takes place everywhere
throughout the school.</i>

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:40.560
<i>Sharing an umbrella emphasizes to onlookers
an intimacy with a member of the opposite sex,</i>

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:41.680
DAMN

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.730
MARKING COMPLETE!!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:43.060
HE'S TAKEN

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.980
<i>and is the most efficient way
to mark someone as being excluded</i>

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.440
<i>from the group
of "summer sweetheart candidates."</i>

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.230
It's really coming down.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.360
Yes. It wasn't raining at all this morning.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.950
<i>There's pretty much one way
that sharing an umbrella works.</i>

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.540
<i>One... "A" has forgotten to bring
an umbrella and is just standing there.</i>

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:04.460
<i>Two... Unable to ignore that,
"B" asks, "Wanna share?"</i>

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:05.460
WANNA SHARE?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:05.460
SUCCESS!!

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.590
Well, should we go?

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.540
<i>In short, the success
of sharing an umbrella...</i>

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:08.540
Yes.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.960
<i>depends on the "I forgot my umbrella" appeal!</i>

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.590
<i>However...</i>

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.300
What should I do?
I don't have an umbrella.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.300
Shoot, I forgot my umbrella.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.970
COMPETITION BATTING!!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:16.970
<i>Batting!</i>

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:22.140
<i>An umbrella sharing event begins
with one person forgetting their umbrella.</i>

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:26.730
<i>But if they both forget their umbrellas,
there are no developments!</i>

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.610
<i>It's just two people
who have forgotten to bring an umbrella!</i>

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.820
Y-You forgot your umbrella, too, Shinomiya?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.700
Yes. It just slipped my mind,
since I usually get picked up.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.030
Why did you forget?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.660
Well, I didn't check the weather forecast.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:43.080
I didn't think
we were in for a storm like this.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.380
<i>Of course, it's all a bluff!</i>

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:52.250
<i>They both have folding umbrellas
in their bags!</i>

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:56.300
<i>What do I do?
Tell her I have an umbrella now?</i>

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.140
<i>But if I do that...</i>

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.470
<i>Oh, my.</i>

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:04.640
<i>You wanted to get under my umbrella
so badly that you lied about your umbrella?</i>

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:06.640
<i>Good grief.</i>

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.690
<i>How cute.</i>

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:09.440
<i>I can't!</i>

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.150
<i>Already, taking out the umbrella
would expose a meaningful lie.</i>

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:17.320
<i>And that would also directly link to inviting
the other person to share the umbrella.</i>

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.780
<i>That would clearly spell defeat.</i>

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.740
<i>Wait. If she doesn't have a ride,</i>

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:26.250
<i>I'm sure someone from the Shinomiya house
would've given her an umbrella.</i>

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.170
<i>It wouldn't matter
that it slipped her mind!</i>

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.380
<i>I've got your number, President.</i>

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:33.300
<i>You have an umbrella
in that bag, don't you?</i>

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.670
<i>You're lying because you're too embarrassed
to invite me under your umbrella.</i>

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.930
<i>In this situation,
the condition for victory...</i>

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:42.180
<i>is none other than exposing
the other person's lie!</i>

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.850
Hey, Shinomiya,
maybe you've actually got one.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.690
<i>Shirogane made the first move.</i>

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:52.690
Your usual ride had a flat today,
on the day it rains.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.690
But today of all days, someone like you,
who always plans ahead, forgot her umbrella.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.200
How likely is that?

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.870
What are you trying to say?

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.200
Oh, nothing.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.000
<i>Not enough information.</i>

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.210
<i>Should I gamble on a game-winning hit?</i>

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:12.210
If we're talking planning ahead,
you do the same, President.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.290
What?

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:19.510
Before, you said you didn't check
the weather forecast, but I find that odd.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:21.260
What's odd about it?

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.720
I have days like that.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.600
You always ride your bicycle
to school, don't you?

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:28.480
Yes, but...

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.230
Then,

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:33.230
why did you take the train today?

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:39.490
I noticed your bike
wasn't in the bike rack today.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.740
<i>What?</i>

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:44.990
I mean, if you think about it,
there's nothing unnatural at all.

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:47.500
On a rainy day,
you take the train to school.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.330
That's the reasonable thing to do, isn't it?

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.790
Say, President...

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:55.380
you said you missed
the weather forecast, right?

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:59.420
Then why did you choose
to take the train today, of all days?

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.430
The truth is...

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.430
you saw it, didn't you?

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:06.970
The weather forecast.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:10.980
<i>The difference in preparation!</i>

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:15.150
Maybe you just thought
you forgot to bring an umbrella.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:19.530
President, would you take a look
in your bag to see if it's there?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.990
<i>The difference in advance preparation
will decide the outcome of the game!</i>

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:27.740
<i>It didn't even take Shirogane an hour
to devise his umbrella-sharing plan.</i>

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.250
<i>On the other hand,
Kaguya confirmed the weather report.</i>

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.870
<i>She carefully looked at the weather map,</i>

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:34.750
<i>used an awl to pierce
the tire of her ride,</i>

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.630
<i>and checked the bicycle rack.</i>

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.000
<i>The amount of advance preparation
gave her a big lead.</i>

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.630
<i>Naturally, she predicted
this situation, as well.</i>

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:44.130
<i>Now I'll score a point for good measure!</i>

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.760
I guess I'll just get soaked
walking home in the rain.

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:52.890
GRIN

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:53.390
Miss Kaguya, you forgot your umbrella?

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:59.400
I've got a spare in the classroom,
so please use this one.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.320
Please be more careful for next time!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.280
Absent-minded Miss Kaguya!

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.410
Well, see ya tomorrow!

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.880
<i>I had him! I was one step away!</i>

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.500
<i>Why does that girl always spoil it?</i>

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.920
<i>Now that it's come to this...</i>

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.220
Here.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.260
I'm giving you this umbrella, President!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.680
Do what you want with it! Here!

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.060
No, that umbrella belongs to Fujiwara.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:33.430
I'm subletting it!

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:34.440
No, look...

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.440
All right.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.700
How about I borrow half of it?

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.460
I suppose that will do.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.480
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:20.480
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:19.020
<i>A tie.</i>

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:20.480
A TIE
